  "question": {
    "text": "An unpolarized light beam is incident on the polarizer of a polarization experiment and the intensity of light beam emerging from the analyzer is measured as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> Lumens. Now, if the analyzer is rotated around the horizontal axis (direction of light) by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> in clockwise direction, the intensity of emerging light will be _______Lumens.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "75",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a754a870-3239-4fd4-a888-4eaf8f6cfd3a-image.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 147px;\" /></p><p>Assuming initially axis of Polarizer and Analyzer are parallel</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/facc8b44-0302-4abe-97ea-87936241d261-image.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 158px;\" /></p><p>Now emerging intensity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math></p>",
